+# R34 UFS rendering / synchronous applog — 2026-11-20
+
+**Priority: next otherwise-identical candidate should disable forced os_log echo for backboardd and SpringBoard.** Logging is a credible critical-path amplifier, not a proved explanation of 99.7 s. User-visible severe lag remains **failed performance acceptance**; input delivery does not establish touch/UI completion. No production patch was applied.
+
+Read-only host inspection, with independent reads in parallel. Only this directory was written. No device/USB/fastboot/adb operations, builds, tests or broad regression/audit. Console searches matched renderer-specific lines only. Input age 34–215 s, 90.65 ms event timestamps versus 99.7 s consumer separation, and the noninitial 99%-busy CPU profile are supplied by main, not independently reconstructed here.
+
+Source prefixes: P = `/home/jia/ios-mix1-build/hakios-lithium-ios16/`; K = `P/xnu-src/xnu-8796.121.2/`; U = `P/userland/`. Coordinates below refer to this actual patched tree.
+
+1. **12–14 ms is the final driver stage, not total UI frame cost.** `K/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:1535–1577,1644–1695` resets the drawing timer after GPU wait and refresh pacing, then measures driver elapsed wall time (including scheduling and in-interval logging). It excludes CA software composition before SwapEnd, queue/idle time, GPU/beat wait, physical scanout, and most of the five-second statistics print. Five seconds is a reporting window, not a sleep.
+
+   Actual renderer line `reports/local/20261120-r34-touch-live-ufs-approved/console.log:6760`: 14 frames / 5168 ms, driver 12273 us, GPU wait 0, beat-wait count 0, held/lost swaps 0/0. That is 2.71 presented frames/s, ~369 ms elapsed per presented frame, but only ~172 ms summed driver intervals (~3.3% of the window). The unassigned remainder is **not measured software-render CPU time**. The supplied 12720-us variant has the same meaning. Line 8917 shows 51/5009 ms (~10/s), so 2–3 FPS is not a demonstrated hard cap. Integer logged FPS truncates. Frame-time histograms classify >=90 ms as pauses (`:89–90,1585–1593`), so their percentiles can hide long gaps.
+
+2. **Software route has no local seconds-long throttle.** `U/src/inject.c:1045–1077` skips EAGL loading at gl=0; `:181–213,513–522` hooks renderer/render_update, caches the first failed acceleration lookup and invokes original render_update directly. Console line 2156 confirms software fallback. The actual software rasterizer and scene scheduler are inside Apple's QuartzCore; these sources do not expose their total cost or prove a low-FPS cap. Historical half-advertised-rate/home-clock-10-Hz comments (`MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:178–189`) are not measurements of this stall.
+
+   Known driver waits: queue full has a 700-ms deadline and held/lost counters (`:91–92,1371–1385`); GPU readiness has a 500-ms bound per surface (`:1541–1547`; fence-dependent implementation `K/iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp:225–235`). Checked renderer windows show no such queue wait and 0-us GPU average. fb_beat defaults on and may wait toward the next ~16.7-ms beat at default 60 Hz (`:1553–1574`). The 40-ms filtered redraw applies only to fb_filter=2, disabled here (`:1420–1428,1486`). An idle presenter sleeps until a swap. SwapWait returns immediately (`:1993–1998`); VSync notifications use a timer and a nonblocking/drop-capable send (`:1870–1876,1903–1909`). No new seconds-long redraw wait was established.
+
+3. **Rendering can progress while input dispatch has not returned.** `U/src/inject.c:1001–1004` creates a detached input pthread. Its serial read loop calls send_touch (`:959–985`), which calls `IOHIDVirtualServiceClientDispatchEvent` inline and ignores its return (`:856`). It does not call the renderer directly. Other backboardd threads and the separate kernel presenter (`MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:1400–1425`) can progress while that thread is inside dispatch or unscheduled; a busy event/scene loop can delay new input-driven updates while unrelated frames continue. This is structural possibility, not proof of current dispatch duration or private framework lock behavior. Initialization sleeps (`inject.c:798–805,936`) are not per-event throttles. Given 90.65 ms timestamps versus 99.7 s consumption, gesture duration does not explain the separation; attribution between dispatch, scheduling, logging and later scene work remains open.
+
+4. **Logging does synchronous work before the asynchronous USB reader.** Exact path:
+
+   - `K/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c:2663–2699,5940–5950`: applog=1 redirects spawn opens of /dev/null for fd1/2 to /dev/console; applog_name matches executable prefixes and injects `OS_ACTIVITY_DT_MODE=YES`, requesting os_log echo to stderr. Injection's own say formats then calls write(2) (`U/src/inject.c:61–73`, SpringBoard `inject_sb.c:63–75`). Proprietary EventFilter formatting/emission and user-space os_log locks are not available here; per-event logging duration is unmeasured.
+   - `/dev/console` delegates to the device (`K/bsd/dev/arm/cons.c:76–79`); `kmwrite` holds the shared TTY mutex across line-discipline write (`K/bsd/dev/arm/km.c:173–180`). `ttwrite` starts output inline and can sleep at high water (`K/bsd/kern/tty.c:2515,2536–2558`), although this driver's immediate drain does not prove that sleep occurred. `kmstart/kmoutput` immediately drains in <=80-byte chunks (`km.c:291–314,353–380`).
+   - `K/osfmk/console/serial_console.c:315–332,399–467,525–586`: ticket write_lock protects console reservations, temporarily disabling preemption; caller can drain inline under flush_lock, blocking for that mutex when space is exhausted. Drain also waits for outstanding reservations and holds flush_lock across output. Formatting, TTY work, these locks and copies are therefore potentially on the logging caller's critical path.
+   - Current `_cnputs` (`serial_console.c:279–290`) bulk-copies through `lithium_log_bytes`: `K/osfmk/arm64/loader_return.c:115–136,168–185` masks IRQ/FIQ, attempts ring lock at most **64 times per <=256 bytes**, copies or drops on contention, and restores DAIF. No USB-acknowledgement wait. Separate single-character/line helpers still contain up to 10,000,000 attempts (`:91–108,146–164`); do not attribute that loop to ordinary bulk stderr. Screen echo is bounded to 4096 characters (`serial_console.c:245–253`); framebuffer text rendering stops on graphics ownership (`K/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c:762–765`). Sustained desktop applog is not proved to be pixel scrolling.
+   - USB is a **separate kernel consumer** (`P/devices/lithium/drivers/usb/hakios.lithium_usb.c:367–382,554–574`), reading retained memory, submitting DMA, handling completion, then sleeping 2 ms. Ring reader uses one try-lock and <=256-byte copy (`loader_return.c:190–216`). Slow host delivery overwrites old retained bytes/loss accounting, not producer host-delivery backpressure. USB still costs CPU and briefly shares the ring lock.
+
+   Consequently, synchronous logging can amplify an EventFilter storm through formatting, syscall/TTY work, shared locks and copies. Neither captured ~2 MB / ~8 min nor aggregate CPU percentages proves or rules out seconds of logging cost. There is no source basis to label the 99.7-s delay a USB-send wait.
+
+5. **Focused next options, unchanged defaults; proposals only.**
+
+   - **First, argument-only candidate:** omit `applog_name=backboardd,SpringBoard`, retain applog=1/stderr and bounded diagnostics; keep display/input/CPU settings identical. Actual generated `U/root/LaunchDaemons/{com.apple.backboardd,com.apple.SpringBoard}.plist` were decoded read-only: both stderr=/dev/console; backboardd has no environment dictionary, SpringBoard only CA_ASSERT_MAIN_THREAD_TRANSACTIONS=1. Neither contains DT_MODE, so removing the boot-arg injection has a concrete target. Beware regeneration: `U/mkjobs.py:270–275,300–302` can independently add DT_MODE via OSLOG; local baseline `upstream/hakios-xnu-kernel/userland/build.sh:468` defaults OSLOG to backboardd. Preserve the actual quiet plist environment. Improvement remains unmeasured.
+   - **If a reusable patch is required:** `applog_ui_quiet` tunable default **0** beside `kern_exec.c:2663`; when explicitly 1, exact-match backboardd/SpringBoard and suppress only forced os_log echo injection at `:2667–2691`. Keep fd routing and other processes unchanged; account for any inherited/job-supplied DT_MODE. This is fact-supported and narrowly scoped.
+   - **If attribution is still needed:** `render_cost=1`, default off, instruments entry/exit of existing begin/render_update/finish hooks (`inject.c:159–213`) into a bounded memory ring with sparse worker aggregates. Similarly aggregate elapsed/lock/drain costs at kmwrite/console_write. No per-event printf; no expensive stack sampling. Current post-return-only lines cannot time a stalled call.
+   - fb_threads1/fb_filter0 are already appropriate for one CPU; helper threads add no CPU. Full equal-size BGRA-to-BGR24 layers take unscaled packing (`MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:862–877,1256`; actual 1080×2040/stride3240 at console line 94). Do not treat driver-thread/filter changes or gl/metal enablement as a fix for unmeasured pre-swap work. Existing ui_lite=1 reduces motion/transparency but synchronizes Data preferences (`U/src/inject_sb.c:819–846`); keep it out of the first logging comparison.
+
+Provenance: patched xnu/files and actual xnu-src copies match SHA256 for framebuffer `d20fcff19ef56dc49b06b5495bc6fd1cee9dc72773e11ab6c798fa7adc29d137` and loader_return `8f1fdcb0dbb7d1a4dd018cae1e3bb6445264a0edd06e89699c1b82c9f3b74a79`. Baseline applog patch is `upstream/hakios-xnu-kernel/xnu/hakios.patch:560–608,809–810`; relevant lithium framebuffer/BGR24/display patches were consulted, with actual patched line coordinates taking precedence. This note does not claim package identity or runtime root-cause proof.
